; Many textures of different sizes that may use system memory (no flag 256) fill the video memory that BLITZLLVM_VRAM_LIMIT_MB leaves, then
; a texture that has to be in video memory makes room by pushing out several of them at once. This is the eviction storm that picks the
; largest textures first; it must end with the big texture made.
Graphics 64, 64, 0, 2
Local i, size
For i = 0 To 95
	size = 256 Shl (i Mod 3)
	CreateTexture(size, size, 1)
Next
CreateTexture(4096, 4096, 1 + 256)
DebugLog "evicted many ok"
End
